    "<font color=\"red\">The chart highlights that the final grade in the second period (G2) is the most influential predictor in the model. Absences also have a modest impact, while other features such as sex, age, health, and parental jobs have minimal influence. This suggests that academic performance in the second period and student attendance are the primary factors in determining the target outcome."
